{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781547368924,"sessionID":"ses_13380d100ffe683zt2nZsCkZT1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2p3v3ig15NWJj7mzb842H1uA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Selection Rules\n2: \n3: Effective date: 2026-05-08\n4: \n5: ## Source Reliability\n6: \n7: - When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n8: - Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n9: - The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n10: \n11: ## First-Wave Requirements\n12: \n13: Select exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n14: \n15: - Region is `North`.\n16: - Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n17: - Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n18: - The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n19: - Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n20: - Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n21: \n22: ## Selection Preference\n23: \n24: - Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n25: - If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n26: - If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","text":"# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n\n## Selection Preference\n\n- Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n- If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n- If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":26,"totalLines":26,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","time":{"start":1781547368565,"end":1781547368845}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0969a058b5dd639e016a304168595081919ba8816c97eb28a5"}},"id":"prt_ecc7f8068001susE9EV3iskeal","sessionID":"ses_13380d100ffe683zt2nZsCkZT1","messageID":"msg_ecc7f4b4b00188XJz0Ht0xY05X"}}
